course: dictionary
lesson: 171
title: Agnostic: not sure, not taking a side
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An agnostic is someone who says we cannot know for sure. Look at the clue in this sentence: «An agnostic is someone who says we cannot know for sure what happens after death.» The words "cannot know for sure" tell you that agnostic means not certain either way.
explain: In religion lessons, three words are set side by side. «An atheist believes there is no God; an agnostic thinks we cannot know whether there is.» A believer says yes, an atheist says no, and an agnostic says we cannot know. Each view is different, and we respect each one.
explain: The word also works as an everyday adjective, meaning not sure or not deciding. «I'm agnostic about pineapple on pizza» means "I have not made up my mind yet." To check, swap in "not sure" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In computer talk, agnostic means "works with any kind of system." «A device-agnostic app» works on any phone or computer, so it does not depend on one special device.
fact: Agnostic means not sure, or not deciding.
fact: An agnostic is a noun for a person, and agnostic is also an adjective: «I'm agnostic about pineapple on pizza.»
fact: In religion and ethics lessons, a believer, an atheist and an agnostic are all different views, and we learn to respect all three.
fact: «A device-agnostic app» works on any phone or computer.
fact: Context clues, such as "cannot know for sure", help you work out what an unknown word means.
exercise: «An agnostic is someone who says we cannot know for sure what happens after death.» What does agnostic mean in this sentence? | *Someone who says we cannot know for sure | Someone who is certain there is no God | Someone who has never heard of death | A person who always chooses a side
exercise: Ellie says, «I'm agnostic about pineapple on pizza.» What does she mean? | She loves pineapple on pizza | She is sure pineapple is the best topping | *She has not made up her mind yet | She hates pizza
exercise: «A device-agnostic app» works on which devices? | Only one special phone | *Any phone or computer | Only computers made in one year | Only tablets with a green screen
test: In a religion lesson, which word means someone who thinks we cannot know whether God exists? | Believer | Teacher | Atheist | *Agnostic
test: «A device-agnostic app works on any phone or computer.» Which word is closest in meaning to agnostic here? | Picky | *Flexible, able to work with any | Expensive | Broken
exam: Which sentence uses agnostic to mean not deciding? | «The agnostic dog ran across the field» | «The agnostic bus leaves at nine o'clock» | «My agnostic shoes are very old» | *«I'm agnostic about the new park, I have not decided yet»
